          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em complex structure
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em integrable
              (see also at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structures"} integrability of G-structures
              the section
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "integrability+of+G-structures#ExampleComplexStructure"} Examples – Complex structure
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#characterizations_of_integrability Characterizations of integrability
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Newlander-Nirenberg+theorem"} Newlander-Nirenberg theorem
            states that an almost complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            on a smooth manifold is integrable (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structures"} integrability of G-structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nijenhuis+tensor"} Nijenhuis tensor
            vanishes,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_J = 0
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structures"} integrability of G-structures
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "integrability+of+G-structures#ExampleComplexStructure"} Examples – Complex structure
          %h3#on_2dimensional_manifolds On 2-dimensional manifolds
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
              on an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              induces an almost complex structure given by forming orthogonal tangent vectors.
          #In2dAnyAlmostComplexStructureIsIntegrable.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Every almost complex structure on a 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              is integrable, hence is a complex structure.
          %p
            In the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+analytic+manifolds"} real analytic manifolds
            this fact was known to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl+Friedrich+Gauss"} Carl Friedrich Gauss
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Audin"} Audin, remark 3 on p. 47
          %h3#relation_to_structures
            Relation to
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
          %p
            Every almost complex structure canonically induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec-structure"} spin^c-structure
            by postcomposition with the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+map"} characteristic map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi c
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi w
                                %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}U(n) &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}Spin^c &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\searrow&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}SO(2n) &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{w}_2}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec-structure"} spin^c-structure
            for more.
          %h3#relation_to_hermitian_and_khler_structure Relation to Hermitian and Kähler structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An almost complex structure equipped with a compatible
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+structure"} Hermitian structure
            %li
              %p
                An almost complex structure equipped with a compatible
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"} Riemannian structure
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+structure"} Kähler structure
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
                %th
                  +
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"} Riemannian structure
                %th
                  +
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+structure"} Hermitian structure
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+structure"} Kähler structure
          %h3#moduli_stacks_of_complex_structures Moduli stacks of complex structures
          %p
            One may consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+complex+structures"} moduli stack of complex structures
            on a given manifold. For 2-dimensional manifolds these are famous as the Riemann
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+complex+curves"} moduli stacks of complex curves
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "moduli+space+of+curves#OverTheComplexNumbers"} here
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+complex+structure"} stable complex structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundle"}> holomorphic vector bundle
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoholomorphic+vector+bundle"} pseudoholomorphic vector bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/para-complex+structure"} para-complex structure
          %h2#references References
          %h3#complex_structure_on_vector_spaces_2 Complex structure on vector spaces
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shoshichi+Kobayashi"}> Shoshichi Kobayashi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katsumi+Nomizu"} Katsumi Nomizu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Foundations of differential geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.wiley.com/en-us/Foundations+of+Differential+Geometry%2C+2+Volume+Set-p-9780470555583"} ISBN:978-0-470-55558-3
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foundations_of_Differential_Geometry"} Wikipedia entry
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_complex_structure"} Linear complex structure
          %p
            Fiberwise complex structure on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundles"} real vector bundles
          %ul
            %li
              Emery Thomas,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Complex Structures on Real Vector Bundles
              %strong 89
              4 (1967) 887-908 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2373409"}> arXiv;10.2307/2373409
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2373409"} jstor:2373409
          %h3#complex_structure_on_manifolds_2 Complex structure on manifolds
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Audin
              Michèle Audin,
              %em Symplectic and almost complex manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-0348-8508-9_3.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+G-structures"} integrable G-structures
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Bryant"}> Robert Bryant
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on the geometry of almost complex 6-manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0508428"} arXiv:math/0508428
          %p A discussion of deformations of complex structures is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              %em
